From 9e71fbace2c35aaf3df212a0cf8ead1fba74998b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ProductSprint Builder <productsprint@local>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 03:54:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add generate-template: real spreadsheet product generation
 (not just listing copy)

- lib/buildSpreadsheet.ts: converts a JSON spec into a real, formatted
  multi-tab .xlsx with live formulas via exceljs, using the same
  navy/gold brand styling as the Freelance Income Tracker listing.
- lib/fallback-spreadsheets.ts: guaranteed non-blank fallback spec,
  following the same pattern as lib/fallback-planners.ts.
- app/api/generate-template/route.ts: new route following the existing
  withUsageCheck -> geminiCall -> extractJson -> cache -> fallback
  pattern used by generate-etsy-pack and generate-planner, but the
  output is the actual downloadable product file (base64 xlsx),
  not marketing copy about it.

This is phase 1 of the 'make ProductSprint build the product, not just
the listing' plan. Verified: standalone exceljs round-trip test confirms
formulas and formatting survive a full write/read cycle; tsc --noEmit
passes clean across the whole project.

Not yet done (next steps):
- UI wiring: no button in IdeaCard/PlannerView calls this route yet.
  Client should POST { idea }, then decode fileBase64 to a Blob and
  trigger a download, same pattern already used in IdeaCard.tsx for
  the .txt etsy-pack export.
- Google Sheets creation (only .xlsx for now) - requires a service
  account + Drive API and is a separate, larger task.
- PDF quick-start guide generation (phase 2, not started).
